<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Kitchens are a considered purchase. Thousands of pounds, months of thinking, and a homeowner who wants to be sure before they commit. That means two things: there's real money in the job, and you need to be one of the fitters they trust while they're deciding. Ads put you in front of them at exactly the right moment.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Full kitchen installations, supply and fit</li>
        <li>Fit-only for supplied kitchens</li>
        <li>Kitchen refurbishments and replacement doors</li>
        <li>Worktops, islands and extensions of existing kitchens</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why real footage wins</h2>
      <p>Nothing sells a kitchen like the reveal. A tired old kitchen turning into a showpiece is exactly the kind of transformation that stops a homeowner scrolling. So we use <strong>real footage of your installs</strong>, filmed on site or from finished jobs, never stock. On a purchase this size, seeing your actual standard of finish is what earns the enquiry.</p>

      <h2>What the funnel asks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Is it a full install, fit-only, or a refurb?</li>
        <li>Are they supplying the kitchen or do they need it supplied too?</li>
        <li>What type of property, and the postcode?</li>
        <li>When are they looking to get it done, and the best number to reach them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That sorts the homeowners with a real budget and a real timeframe from the ones just gathering ideas, so you spend your evenings quoting genuine jobs.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
    </div>

